{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lg0xv23r","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline","year":2007,"examDate":2007,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"polymers","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pmatch-the-chemical-substances-in-column-i-with-type-of-po-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-3aki3lgxvhn5x73m","content":"<p>Match the chemical substances in Column I with type of polymers/type of bonds in Column II. Indicate your answer by darkening the appropriate bubbles of the 4 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 4 matrix given in the ORS.</p>\n<p>\n<table class=\"tg\" style=\"undefined;table-layout: fixed; width: 472px\">\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 48px\">\n<col style=\"width: 192px\">\n<col style=\"width: 53px\">\n<col style=\"width: 179px\">\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n  <tr>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\">Column I</th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\">Column II</th>\n  </tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(A)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">cellulose</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(P)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">natural polymer</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(B)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">nylon-6, 6</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(Q)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">synthetic polymer</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(C)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">protein</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(R)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">amide linkage</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(D)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">sucrose</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(S)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">glycoside linkage</td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"A - (p, s); B - (q); C - (p, r); D - (s)"},{"identifier":"B","content":"A - (p, s); B - (q, r); C - (r); D - (s)"},{"identifier":"C","content":"A - (p, s); B - (q, r); C - (p, r); D - (s)"},{"identifier":"D","content":"A - (s); B - (q, r); C - (p, r); D - (s)"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>(A) Cellulose - a natural polymer of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-D-glucose, linked by glycoside linkage.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mggooc8c/9c964806-7c64-46da-a3fb-14c8e955e47f/e804f2c0-a38d-11f0-9d8c-33e535796787/file-jaoe38c1mggooc8d.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mggooc8c/9c964806-7c64-46da-a3fb-14c8e955e47f/e804f2c0-a38d-11f0-9d8c-33e535796787/file-jaoe38c1mggooc8d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Polymers Question 4 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1mggooc8c/9c964806-7c64-46da-a3fb-14c8e955e47f/e804f2c0-a38d-11f0-9d8c-33e535796